F4 Medium | The directory-replacement heal is incomplete on the EVENT path. The `arm()` guard compares only the inode; an `rm -rf <dir>` + `mkdir <dir>` reuses the freed inode on this filesystem, so the dead watch is treated as 'already armed' and kept. The FSWatcher has already emitted `close` (IN_IGNORED) and `watching` still reports true. Rename-away produces no notification at all, so `arm()` never runs; the writer's own arm calls `poll()` explicitly, and NO product caller does. | where packages/mpd-graph-core/src/watch.ts — `arm()`'s `ino === entry.ino` check and `armDirectory()` (no `close`/liveness tracking). | observed replace-trials.txt: rm-recreate 3/3 sameIno=true, replacementDelivered=1, late write delivered=1 (missed); rename-away 2/2 deliveredAfterReplace=0. debug-close-event.ts: the deleted directory's FSWatcher emits 'close' (IN_IGNORED) while our map keeps `watching` true. Writer's arm: `packages/mpd-graph-core/test/watch.test.ts` 'the watch follows the NEW inode' calls `watcher.poll()` between the rename and the new write. | direction Track the armed handle's LIVENESS, not just its inode: subscribe to the FSWatcher's `close` event and mark the entry dead so the next `arm()` re-arms it; or compare `birthtimeMs` in addition to `ino`; either way add an arm that uses the rm+recreate shape and does NOT call poll() before the late write.
